From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] scheduler: balance async PP decode batches (aligns upstream #57433)

Model Runner V2 + pipeline parallelism + async scheduling lets a decode request
advance only once every `pp_size` scheduler steps, because the worker-side
sampled-token broadcast ring consumes a step-T result at T+pp_size (#42187).
Nothing spreads the running set over those in-flight batches, so requests whose
prefills complete in the same step lock into one cadence group and then advance
and starve together. #50853 lists this as an open gap; #57433 fixes it upstream
with a decode-only per-step share of `ceil(max_num_seqs / pp_size)`.

This patch is that upstream implementation, ported to our pinned source, with
one deliberate deviation: upstream applies it unconditionally for MRV2 +
AsyncScheduler + PP>1, while here it is gated behind VLLM_PP_DECODE_COHORT_BALANCE
(default ON). Reason for shipping it on: measured on PP6 with a same-image A/B that varied only this switch, 3 repeats per cell, aggregate tok/s, acceptance unchanged - prose +19.3% at c16 and +77.8% at c32, counting +48.9% and +78.7%. Setting VLLM_PP_DECODE_COHORT_BALANCE=0 restores upstream behaviour, so rollback stays one env var plus a restart.

Everything else matches #57433 structurally rather than only semantically, so a
future pin bump can drop this patch without a rewrite:

  * the policy lives in `_get_max_num_scheduled_decodes()`, defined on Scheduler
    (returns max_num_running_reqs, so PP1 / sync / MRV1 keep the old effective
    limit) and overridden on AsyncScheduler;
  * the cohort set is a local of schedule(), not scheduler state, so a step can
    never inherit a stale count;
  * the cap sits immediately before KV block allocation in the RUNNING loop, and
    established decodes resumed from WAITING are capped too (skipped via
    step_skipped_waiting, like the other cannot-schedule-now cases);
  * preemption discards the cohort slot it had taken;
  * `assert len(scheduled_decode_req_ids) <= max_num_scheduled_decodes` guards
    the invariant at the end of the step.

Prefill, chunked prefill and the chunk that completes a prompt in this step stay
uncapped, which is the whole reason this form was chosen over the global request
cap in #50410: per that thread the global cap measured -8.21% throughput and
+11.31% mean TTFT against doing nothing, while the decode-only form measured
+22.95%.

Signed-off-by: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
